the weekly FAQ _suggests_ that wizard-mode can be entered by
    nethack -u wizard -D
or other similar permutations.  this is only a suggestion because
site installers configure this option to taste.  also, the mac port
does not have a command line, so the above suggestion is irrelevant.
i don't have the FAQ handy but the author (obviously brilliant)
worded it correctly ...

the owner's manual is supposed to accompany the mac port.  maybe you
didn't get it.  here's a snippet from nh30j.doc (obtained as advised
from the FAQ):

****************
...
Macintosh NetHack 3.0j3 (patchlevel 10) Manual
last modified July 20, 1991
...
This document, "nh30j3.doc", should also accompany the Macintosh
NetHack 3.0 package.
...
Wizard-mode play
================
Wizard-mode gives the user additional powers for debugging the
game.  Abusing the privileges of wizard-mode will spoil your game.
Therefore you should reserve using this mode only for debugging purposes.
Wizard-mode, normally inaccessible, has commands
appropriately documented under the "?" help command.  To activate
wizard-mode you have two options: 1) express or 2) traditional:

express access:
Hold down 3 of the 4 modifier keys (control, option, shift or
command) while launching NetHack (pl10 only).  Release the keys
when the "About" dialog finally appears.  If there is no saved
wizard file then a random character type will be chosen for you.

traditional access:
1) Start a normal game.
2) Change the default name in the "Set Options..." entry of the
    File menu to "wizard".  Click "Save" to record the change.
3) Quit (or save) the game and start another (not a save file).
4) Use the name "wizard" in the starting dialog box.  The normally
    hidden wizard-mode check box will now be revealed.  You can
    also choose a character type on the opening dialog.
5) During wizard-mode play remember to change your name on the
    "options" dialog back to your default preference for
    subsequent normal games.
****************

about the unix version, the site installer has to configure config.h
as indicated in the `Install.???' documents.  here's the relevant
snippet from config.h:

****************
#ifndef WIZARD		/* allow for compile-time or Makefile changes */
# ifndef KR1ED
#define WIZARD  "izchak" /* the person allowed to use the -D option */
# else
#define WIZARD
#define WIZARD_NAME "izchak"
# endif
#endif
****************

apparently, the developers wanted all the micro ports to have the
same wizard name (i.e. "wizard") but they fumbled since "Wizard"
is also used (note: case is important).  for unix ports, and the
like, "izchak" should be changed to the maintainers account name.
nethack -u izchak -D
shouldn't work, in this case, because the wizard name is compared
to various things including your login name.

